    skos:broader categories:vegetables ;
    skos:definition "Scallions (green onions) are vegetables of various Allium onion species. Spring onions may be cooked or used raw as a part of salads, salsas or Asian recipes. Diced scallions are used in soup, noodle and seafood dishes, sandwiches, curries and as part of a stir fry. In many Eastern sauces, the bottom half-centimetre (quarter-inch) of the root is commonly removed before use."@en ;
